 ### [Level-of-detail (LOD) methods](1007-level-of-detail-lod-methods.md)
-Level-of-detail (LOD) methods are techniques for interactive visualization of large scalar fields that maintain responsive frame rates by generating reduced-resolution approximations of the original data during user interaction. Unlike static resolution schemes, these methods dynamically adjust the rendering quality based on performance metrics or visual error, switching to higher quality representations only when necessary. They are distinguished from sibling methods like [Dynamic Volume Resolution & Alpha Mask Update](2539-dynamic-volume-resolution-alpha-mask-update.md) by their primary focus on temporal adaptability during interaction rather than static spatial partitioning or alpha-mask-driven culling. See [Level-of-detail (LOD) methods](1007-level-of-detail-lod-methods.md).
+Level-of-detail (LOD) methods maintain interactive frame rates during viewpoint interaction by dynamically changing the resolution of the rendering to match the available computational budget. Unlike static pre-computed LOD hierarchies, these methods adapt the sampling density or geometric approximation in real-time based on rendering performance metrics. This approach solves the problem of high computational cost in volume rendering by trading visual fidelity for speed during interactive manipulation, switching to higher quality only when the view is static or when the frame budget allows.
 
 ### [Dynamic Volume Resolution & Alpha Mask Update](2539-dynamic-volume-resolution-alpha-mask-update.md)
-This method dynamically adjusts the voxel grid resolution and the active spatial bounding box (AABB) of a neural volume representation during training. It solves the problem of inefficient memory usage and slow convergence by initially training in a low-resolution, coarse space and progressively refining the grid density and spatial extent as the model learns. It differs from static resolution methods by coupling resolution upscaling with alpha mask updates, ensuring that the volume only occupies the space containing visible geometry, thereby pruning empty background space. See [Dynamic Volume Resolution & Alpha Mask Update](2539-dynamic-volume-resolution-alpha-mask-update.md).
